        <p>{item.body}</p>
      </div>
    ))}
  </div>

  <p>
    None of these tracks is objectively "the best" one. IT-services breadth is a genuine asset if
    you are still deciding which domain to specialise in later. Banking, insurance, and healthcare
    depth compounds faster into higher pay and trust, but locks you in more tightly — moving
    sectors later means partially rebuilding that domain credibility from a lower rung. Product-company
    BSA work pays well but demands a technical floor (SQL, dashboards) that a pure requirements-and-
    documentation BA does not need to clear.
  </p>

