  </div>

  <p>
    Not every strong BA needs or wants this bridge. Senior BA and lead BA roles, and eventually
    strategy or advisory work, are real, well-paying destinations on their own that build directly on
    domain trust and requirement-ownership without needing the product-management retrain. A smaller
    number of experienced BAs also move into independent process-consulting work for small and
    mid-sized businesses once their domain reputation is strong enough to attract clients directly —
    a genuine but slower-building leverage path that trades employer stability for higher day-rate
    potential. Choose the lane based on which weekly work you actually want a decade of, not on which
    title sounds more advanced on LinkedIn.
  </p>

